[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198580 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198384 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "58fbdce5-60b9-5682-a84e-1c8a5077c762" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Image of a Horizontal Segment Under a Polar Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9b4c5e4-e959-56e2-a295-57ff1957f4c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459587} {:answer/id #uuid "35bc7942-5cb9-5f6e-a604-01bbc56e91d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35bc7942-5cb9-5f6e-a604-01bbc56e91d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459588} :answer-field/id #uuid "34d30ed0-77d5-5679-93b2-0ea48f44edef" :answer-field/key "The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ with the positive $x$-axis." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460660} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6680343a-55ac-5674-af4a-41f728522fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459589} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea09bb3-fab5-5fa4-9de9-6cc3c6ceedb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459590}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6680343a-55ac-5674-af4a-41f728522fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459589} :answer-field/id #uuid "a56b6579-beea-5a72-b0d9-20005a09ab04" :answer-field/key "The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ with the positive $x$-axis." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460661} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88a4ac9d-8c4a-5b91-b0b8-c3f46a3d66a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459591} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3da9de-0754-5c44-b6f9-c2f9e21352c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88a4ac9d-8c4a-5b91-b0b8-c3f46a3d66a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459591} :answer-field/id #uuid "323a6fc7-1616-52bd-a614-a99166c8c0e4" :answer-field/key "The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $1$ and $2$ centered at $O.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460662} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a9c7d82-48a5-5082-9db0-75f593adafce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667972} {:answer/id #uuid "40783646-3c4c-5b29-bcfb-76294fc2b2d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a9c7d82-48a5-5082-9db0-75f593adafce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667972} :answer-field/id #uuid "9937218a-ae78-5443-b03a-a3a51e71f6b3" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668263}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9eb2357b-f9d2-552f-8ddb-db8ea02b5422" :question/math-academy-id "q-160481" :question/problem "![](images/b8/b8874b14fa80881e69cb1daee180d2e342a27c5902e66fc75d43622278176b09.png)\n\nConsider the square region $Δ$ in the $uv$-plane, given by\n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(u,v)\\,:\\,1\\le u\\le \\sqrt{2},\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}\\},\n$$\n\nand the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:(u,v)\\to (u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v).\n$$\n\nThe image of the bottom side of $Δ$ under the action of $T$ is a line segment. Which of the following statements are true regarding the image?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To map the entire region $Δ$ onto the $xy$-plane, we consider the transformation of each side. However, in this case, we consider only the bottom side.\n\nFor the bottom side, we have $v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $1\\le u\\le \\sqrt{2}.$ \n\nSubstituting $v=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ into our transformation equations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x,y) & =T(u,v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v) \\\\  & =(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right),\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)),\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le v\\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is a parametric equation of the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/fc/fcfc165548d8174ec0468dce53317fd0c8daa14565852c5e44d6764161723bed.png)\n\n \n\nNote that the line that this segment lies on passes through the origin. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ with the positive $x$-axis” is true, while statement “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ with the positive $x$-axis” is false. The slope of the line is\n\n$$\nk=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)}=\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right).\n$$\n\nAs a result, our line makes an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ radians with the positive $x$-axis.\n\n- Statement “The endpoints of the image lie on the circles of radii $1$ and $2$ centered at $O.$” is false.\n\n- When $u=1,$ we obtain the point \n$(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $1.$\n\n- When $u=\\sqrt{2},$ we obtain the point \n$(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right),\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right)),$\nwhose distance to the origin is $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo, the endpoints of the line segment lie on the circles of radii $1$ and $\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The image makes the angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ with the positive $x$-axis” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198721 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aa2f2ccb-45b0-5d6a-aa94-ac3eb95c745b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Predicates of More Than One Variable"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "704e020e-d34a-528d-9e9d-8b82289223c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459647} {:answer/id #uuid "f766b986-cfca-589d-b307-c3cfed4a40df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f766b986-cfca-589d-b307-c3cfed4a40df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459648} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8358696-c4dc-5792-a56d-b4cf06cd1f4e" :answer-field/key "$x<y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f32f7ace-9473-5adf-87d1-3a0754c1f4bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459649} {:answer/id #uuid "5764e144-7231-5741-8902-987088781ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5764e144-7231-5741-8902-987088781ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459650} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c262398-01aa-5334-93fb-2d94d63b0e3f" :answer-field/key "$n$ is a perfect square." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0937afd-eb79-5420-8b9b-1cc18cc13046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459651} {:answer/id #uuid "971d785f-c08d-59dc-8767-b018db2c3a8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0937afd-eb79-5420-8b9b-1cc18cc13046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459651} :answer-field/id #uuid "45cf6747-f781-581e-9df2-b7717fa5597b" :answer-field/key "Are $n$ and $m$ coprime?" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460692} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d3f2064-e567-5631-bd96-9557ad8ce599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667980} {:answer/id #uuid "7a0a260b-dae8-5562-b7bc-09d648ba2610" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d3f2064-e567-5631-bd96-9557ad8ce599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667980} :answer-field/id #uuid "47bba079-fd67-5b5b-9ddb-59324116c906" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d3a9664a-054f-5dcf-9b0e-e1b4ab3dd171" :question/math-academy-id "q-174456" :question/problem "Which of the following are mathematical predicates?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *predicate* of the variables ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}$ is a sentence that contains the variables defined on some *universal set*, and has the property that when we substitute concrete values for all the variables into the predicate, the result becomes a statement that is either true or false.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our options. \n\n- Option $x<y$ is a predicate of two variables. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(x,y)$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option “$n$ is a perfect square” is a predicate of one variable. Substituting a concrete value for $n$ into the sentence, we get a statement that is either true or false.\n\n- Option “Are $n$ and $m$ coprime?” is *not* a predicate. Substituting a concrete pair of values $(n,m)$ into the sentence, we do not get a statement that is either true or false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x<y$; “$n$ is a perfect square” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6dfedbf-e8f5-5c35-ac7a-3280352e020a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459653} {:answer/id #uuid "e9713a4a-6827-5ab4-8250-e0c6662fd257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9713a4a-6827-5ab4-8250-e0c6662fd257" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459654} :answer-field/id #uuid "a72b8fb7-3248-5357-886c-14a9921e2b27" :answer-field/key "${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b51687-e975-5fef-b586-123a8d03457c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459655} {:answer/id #uuid "4719370a-40fe-5819-95db-2750f3e9f8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4719370a-40fe-5819-95db-2750f3e9f8ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459656} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a2ed651-b0b2-5578-8e7f-41bdc35291ec" :answer-field/key "${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb6b8dbf-9094-5908-9192-5e790c2e9227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459657} {:answer/id #uuid "429f461b-d81f-54c3-bf90-863669545081" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459658}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb6b8dbf-9094-5908-9192-5e790c2e9227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459657} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fb97e7e-61b1-52f5-b06e-85a2025b70ce" :answer-field/key "${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4dceea4-5a37-5938-8648-c38edf776958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667982} {:answer/id #uuid "019b0657-54bb-57b8-921f-6c1a1ada4167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667983}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4dceea4-5a37-5938-8648-c38edf776958" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667982} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba1c73be-09ed-57ab-92f6-757a3d627225" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668268}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "70a4471c-4be9-5243-a617-e32ac5259d39" :question/math-academy-id "q-177075" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}=18-18=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal” is true. Indeed, $Q({u}_{1})⊥Q({u}_{2})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{2})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal” is false. Notice that, for example, $Q({u}_{1})$ is not a unit vector since\n\n$$\n‖Q({u}_{1})‖=‖{u}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{{9}^{2}+{6}^{2}}\\ne 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$; “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198449 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b4a5d6b1-e76a-5b33-8973-04d1d9062dc6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Orthogonality of a Two-Vector Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dbc2877-1064-59e1-91d9-6e3ec0e08661" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459659} {:answer/id #uuid "96fa23cc-f15c-5d76-81ac-bc08e6bb7e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "96fa23cc-f15c-5d76-81ac-bc08e6bb7e90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459660} :answer-field/id #uuid "17e2d61d-61b6-527d-afb9-3443e06829eb" :answer-field/key "${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "298a33f1-a9b2-595a-9ecb-d624448c5ff0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459661} {:answer/id #uuid "a83a64fc-53ec-556f-b18a-e94d5ea6215f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a83a64fc-53ec-556f-b18a-e94d5ea6215f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459662} :answer-field/id #uuid "18b4689d-0aaf-5f9c-af23-436c85c48526" :answer-field/key "${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd291524-b945-53dc-9025-02857a4bfebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459663} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac8bba8-265c-5892-93e3-19c51777ca3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459664}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ac8bba8-265c-5892-93e3-19c51777ca3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459664} :answer-field/id #uuid "30a33278-fdbc-523a-bfa4-2f8a09609b7d" :answer-field/key "${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460698} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2731dc14-1665-5886-bdd9-cbb72ead4f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667984} {:answer/id #uuid "56dac323-7346-502a-916c-8d3351a70040" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2731dc14-1665-5886-bdd9-cbb72ead4f62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667984} :answer-field/id #uuid "e14f25c8-0330-5a12-9215-35acf7fef220" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668269}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6d806a7-8383-51f7-a460-be3b003d424b" :question/math-academy-id "q-177315" :question/problem "$$\n{u}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the vectors above, and let $Q$ be an orthogonal linear transformation. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $Q$ is orthogonal, we have that $Q(x)\\cdot Q(y)=x\\cdot y$ for any vectors $x$ and $y.$\n\nThe linear transformation $Q$ being orthogonal is equivalent to the following:\n\n- The matrix $Q$ of transformation $Q$ relative to any orthonormal basis (including the standard basis) of ${R}^{n}$ is orthogonal.\n\n- $||Q(x)||=||x||.$\n\n- If $x⊥y$ then $Q(x)⊥Q(y)$ for any $x,y\\in {R}^{n}.$ In general, $Q$ preserves the angle between any two vectors.\n\n- $Q$ maps any orthogonal (orthonormal) set into an orthogonal (orthonormal) set.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$ is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal” is true. Indeed, $Q({u}_{1})⊥Q({u}_{2})$ since\n\n$$\nQ({u}_{1})\\cdot Q({u}_{2})={u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal” is true. Indeed, both $Q({u}_{1})$ and $Q({u}_{2})$ are unit vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖Q({u}_{1})‖ & =‖{u}_{1}‖=\\sqrt{\\left(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2}+\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2}}=1 \\\\ ‖Q({u}_{2})‖ & =‖{u}_{2}‖=\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2}+\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)^{2}}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0$; “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthogonal”; “${Q({u}_{1}),Q({u}_{2})}$ is orthonormal”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229632 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4823cf5-2656-5616-b4af-193f70c3f2bc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Euler's Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "57aa916c-bfce-5176-a728-d130b05e8b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462255} {:answer/id #uuid "4364076f-372e-558b-952d-afe7f8f775fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57aa916c-bfce-5176-a728-d130b05e8b5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462255} :answer-field/id #uuid "6412fb02-5380-5123-a4ed-d95732ca3e44" :answer-field/key "$Δx=0.05$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462881} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec43a88-ab6d-58a6-a064-9eeeb595fc02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462257} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bef18a-3eb2-5854-8301-ad9cc3b229d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3bef18a-3eb2-5854-8301-ad9cc3b229d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462258} :answer-field/id #uuid "f71fa51b-e9ad-54fb-bc84-e63e7f534858" :answer-field/key "$Δx=0.12$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "daf05c42-176b-5a24-b42d-4314a6a83db0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462259} {:answer/id #uuid "3cad80ec-3d09-5f8d-97d8-c7931d449f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462260}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cad80ec-3d09-5f8d-97d8-c7931d449f25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462260} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8a3446e-4a5a-5b0c-9306-1db8ca0e99b6" :answer-field/key "$Δx=0.2$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462883} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6ba6fb0-4f67-5aa0-9fb5-9cf961718d38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462261} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a06492-23fe-568c-915a-316ad54a2a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a06492-23fe-568c-915a-316ad54a2a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462262} :answer-field/id #uuid "af8b5bf0-28cc-54aa-b3df-3c4021ef6369" :answer-field/key "$Δx=0.25$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "509ebcbd-fa10-5ab6-aaf1-e025885aede1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668006} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb329a0-4a44-5d63-af0a-affa3bc9f5b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "509ebcbd-fa10-5ab6-aaf1-e025885aede1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668006} :answer-field/id #uuid "15ada070-1192-5a98-980e-731709e45490" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9a565f18-6ab5-54a7-92a6-bb08c51a36fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-332461" :question/problem "For which of the following step sizes is Euler's Method **unstable**, given that $\\lambda =20$ is the parameter of the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda >0,$ and step size $Δx?$\n\n*Hint: The stability function for Euler's method is given by* $R(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nFor stability, we require that the following condition holds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(\\lambda Δx)| & <1 \\\\ |1-\\lambda Δx| & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this gives\n\n$$\n0<\\lambda Δx<2.\n$$\n\nThis means that Euler's method is stable when applied to the test equation for values in the region $0<\\lambda Δx<2.$\n\nIn our case, where $\\lambda =20,$ this region simplifies to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & <20Δx<2 \\\\ 0 & <Δx<\\frac{2}{20} \\\\ 0 & <Δx<0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, of the given step sizes:\n\n- $Δx=0.05$ *satisfies* the inequality,\n\n- $Δx=0.12$ *doesn't satisfy* the inequality,\n\n- $Δx=0.2$ *doesn't satisfy* the inequality, and\n\n- $Δx=0.25$ *doesn't satisfy* the inequality.\n\nHence, Euler's method is unstable for the step sizes $Δx=0.12,$ $Δx=0.2,$ and $Δx=0.25.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $Δx=0.12$; $Δx=0.2$; $Δx=0.25$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229636 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229159 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d4823cf5-2656-5616-b4af-193f70c3f2bc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Euler's Method"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a567c91c-11d7-5940-8adc-f09cd2d0fddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462263} {:answer/id #uuid "31e3f346-f2a6-5edb-91d3-5031fb7f980a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462264}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31e3f346-f2a6-5edb-91d3-5031fb7f980a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462264} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fcd9ee7-351d-5544-b31e-d5339038bd16" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.67$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ffee5da-bd54-550d-bf31-632cd5a50672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462265} {:answer/id #uuid "76edda26-bda9-5fec-afe7-b