r-field/id #uuid "7225a2f4-1737-5b07-bd07-4b0019b5b353" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=2.25$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc69a1c1-0171-504e-b1d8-3bf4b2281c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668008} {:answer/id #uuid "ff408051-56de-5f6f-839e-388a6bb9d087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668009}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc69a1c1-0171-504e-b1d8-3bf4b2281c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668008} :answer-field/id #uuid "82b04cbe-4e1b-5875-b8e1-59c6fdc2b580" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668281}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3afc7fc5-d735-57e5-883a-73d956edd87b" :question/math-academy-id "q-332533" :question/problem "For which of the following values is Euler's method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation ${y}^{′}=-\\lambda y$ with $y=y(x),y(0)=1,x\\ge 0,\\lambda >0,$ and step size $Δx?$\n\n*Hint: The stability function for Euler's method is given by* $R(\\lambda Δx)=1-\\lambda Δx.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nFor stability, we require that the following condition holds:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(\\lambda Δx)| & <1 \\\\ |1-\\lambda Δx| & <1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this gives\n\n$$\n0<\\lambda Δx<2.\n$$\n\nThis means that Euler's method is stable when applied to the test equation for values in the region $0<\\lambda Δx<2.$ Of the given values:\n\n- $\\lambda Δx=0.67$ falls *within* the given region,\n\n- $\\lambda Δx=1.20$ falls *within* the given region,\n\n- $\\lambda Δx=1.80$ falls *within* the given region, and\n\n- $\\lambda Δx=2.25$ falls *outside* the given region.\n\nHence, Euler's method is stable for the values $\\lambda Δx=0.67,$ $\\lambda Δx=1.20,$ and $\\lambda Δx=1.80.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\lambda Δx=0.67$; $\\lambda Δx=1.20$; $\\lambda Δx=1.80$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229645 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229161 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "151add00-204f-5795-aff9-cceddc26b24b" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Stability in Other Methods"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c75b2618-e58f-5a5e-a07d-4506f39e76ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462271} {:answer/id #uuid "59444dcb-d81a-5688-9295-c45af0528631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462272}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59444dcb-d81a-5688-9295-c45af0528631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462272} :answer-field/id #uuid "e760dc06-4f39-5008-9111-997359c6c062" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=0.25$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462889} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eff86d2c-8530-55e1-a6af-98da9b6b7e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462273} {:answer/id #uuid "66f87dbb-9705-5fe1-a860-41d5650de70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462274}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66f87dbb-9705-5fe1-a860-41d5650de70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462274} :answer-field/id #uuid "08fbd06e-5a9c-5247-a8e2-41e11a434499" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462890} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df031eda-13a3-5275-85ef-18626f09d51d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462275} {:answer/id #uuid "02e8178f-123f-5ac2-b8ba-7b9aee11f74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462276}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02e8178f-123f-5ac2-b8ba-7b9aee11f74c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462276} :answer-field/id #uuid "f93f3e78-13df-57f3-9c46-4fdd8658adc6" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=1.5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462891} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9eeb3051-767c-5ffd-8d81-1bef7228a039" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462277} {:answer/id #uuid "4b06c67d-b553-51b6-84b1-c10e1d0433f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b06c67d-b553-51b6-84b1-c10e1d0433f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462278} :answer-field/id #uuid "aee7d0a1-c6d4-5302-9a71-d85e3fffc228" :answer-field/key "$\\lambda Δx=9$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462892} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "234144be-d77c-58d5-b03e-dd23c379f148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668010} {:answer/id #uuid "fc4759a1-aa75-5d0a-b1f7-44d387408cce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668011}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "234144be-d77c-58d5-b03e-dd23c379f148" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668010} :answer-field/id #uuid "86a700f7-14fc-5b8e-b829-aaea90b17b80" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddd8726a-dc80-58fb-bcd2-049555ab4372" :question/math-academy-id "q-332737" :question/problem "For which of the following values is the implicit Euler method stable, given that $\\lambda $ is the parameter of the test equation?\n\n*Hint: The stability function $R$ of the implicit Euler method is given by*\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δ)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "A numerical method\n${y}_{n+1}={y}_{n}+Δ{y}_{n}$\nis stable for a given step size $Δx$ if, when applied to the test equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-\\lambda y,\\,y(0)=1,\\,x\\ge 0,\\,\\lambda >0,\n$$\n\nthe numerical solution satisfies ${y}_{n}\\to 0$ as $n\\to \\infty ,$ just like the exact solution.\n\nWhen a method is applied to the test equation, the update takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{n+1}=R(\\lambda Δx){y}_{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $R(\\lambda Δx)$ is referred to as the stability function of the method. The set of values for which the method is stable, given by $|R(\\lambda Δx)|<1,$ is called the stability region of the method.\n\nThe stability function of the implicit Euler method is\n\n$$\nR(\\lambda Δx)=\\frac{1}{1+\\lambda Δx}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the stability of the Implicit Euler Method for each of the given values in turn.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=0.25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(0.25)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+0.25}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{1.25}| \\\\  & =0.8<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+1}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{2}| \\\\  & =0.5<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=1.5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(1.5)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+1.5}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{2.5}| \\\\  & =0.4<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\n- For $\\lambda Δx=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|R(9)| & =|\\frac{1}{1+9}| \\\\  & =|\\frac{1}{10}| \\\\  & =0.1<1.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince this value falls *within* the stability region, the implicit Euler method is stable.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\lambda Δx=0.25$; $\\lambda Δx=1$; $\\lambda Δx=1.5$; $\\lambda Δx=9$.\n\nNote that, since the implicit Euler method is absolutely stable, it is stable for all possible values of $\\lambda Δx.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229667 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbefb3bb-4783-5d77-b404-1f43ee8765de" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Cases Where Differentiating Under the Integral Sign Applies"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6558891a-309c-5fcc-9f