#edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462302}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e4e4108-caef-5eb5-8b0c-8577bd8619ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462301} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ef5c77-471e-59c1-81eb-fd6c4c2a4d56" :answer-field/key "${F}_{3}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}|x-t|\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\ge 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462904} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19c9e073-ac24-57d6-8c99-2f9c2786ac0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668016} {:answer/id #uuid "40c48110-c9b1-5bb4-ac05-7aa7112b527c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "19c9e073-ac24-57d6-8c99-2f9c2786ac0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668016} :answer-field/id #uuid "0b281a7e-7116-53d5-861c-55afc8d0e671" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668285}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ba9a4b07-0b33-5dc7-adcc-95cbc6ada4ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-334667" :question/problem "For which of the following functions is it valid to differentiate under the integral sign?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each function:\n\n- For the first function, we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(x,t)={e}^{tx}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe fix ${t}_{0}\\in R$ and choose $c<{t}_{0}<d,$ so $R=[0,1]\\times [c,d].$\n\nNote that ${f}_{1}$ is continuous on $R.$ Computing the partial derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂t}=x{e}^{tx}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nwhich exists and is continuous on $R.$ Thus, differentiating under the integral sign is valid at ${t}_{0}.$ And since our choice of ${t}_{0}$ was arbitrary, we can compute ${F}_{1}^{′}(t)$ for all real $t.$\n\n- For the second function, we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{2}(x,t)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe fix ${t}_{0}>1$ and choose $[c,d]⊂[1,\\infty )$ such that $c<{t}_{0}<d,$ so $R=[0,1]\\times [c,d].$\n\nNote that ${f}_{2}$ is continuous on $R$ (since the denominator never vanishes on $R$). Computing the partial derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂t}=-\\frac{2t{x}^{2}}{({x}^{2}+{t}^{2})^{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich exists and is continuous on $R.$ Thus, differentiating under the integral sign is valid at ${t}_{0}.$ And since our choice of ${t}_{0}$ was arbitrary, we can compute ${F}_{2}^{′}(t)$ for all real $t\\ge 1.$\n\n- For the third function, we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x,t)=|x-t|.\n$$\n\nWe fix ${t}_{0}\\in (0,1)$ and choose $c<{t}_{0}<d$ such that $[c,d]⊆[0,1],$ so $R=[0,1]\\times [c,d].$\n\nNote that ${f}_{3}$ is continuous on $R.$ However, the partial derivative\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂t}={\\begin{aligned}-1,\\,x>t \\\\ 1,\\,x<t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndoes *not* exist whenever $x=t={t}_{0},$ and is therefore not defined everywhere on $R.$ Thus, differentiating under the integral sign is *not* valid.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${F}_{1}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{tx}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\in R$; ${F}_{2}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\ge 1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229680 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229192 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bbefb3bb-4783-5d77-b404-1f43ee8765de" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Cases Where Differentiating Under the Integral Sign Applies"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf63ad57-9357-5291-8c54-2bac509200e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462303} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4dec50-d253-51c8-a8ab-d8fac88110b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462304}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd4dec50-d253-51c8-a8ab-d8fac88110b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462304} :answer-field/id #uuid "6da89e05-9105-598c-8708-b1ac4df35e21" :answer-field/key "${F}_{1}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(tx)\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462905} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cbfe56b-3d4a-5658-ba44-dad05d46d3d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462305} {:answer/id #uuid "54cfdfa4-fe9b-5c51-9403-a36ef555621e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54cfdfa4-fe9b-5c51-9403-a36ef555621e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462306} :answer-field/id #uuid "c26a7213-042f-57ab-b3b9-dcb3d7edcfb5" :answer-field/key "${F}_{2}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x-t)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\in R$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85068b9f-a046-599c-b6e2-e0ec372733f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462307} {:answer/id #uuid "6dbbdd07-a058-597b-911e-e570ca15e765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dbbdd07-a058-597b-911e-e570ca15e765" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462308} :answer-field/id #uuid "d776c753-b8c3-5917-9fca-75596c7bf274" :answer-field/key "${F}_{3}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{x-t}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t<0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462907} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029f3773-976b-5cfb-9eb0-ee8ced25be1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668018} {:answer/id #uuid "bd62e6c1-3988-56a9-8b5e-b59a21e8400b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "029f3773-976b-5cfb-9eb0-ee8ced25be1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668018} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd85216f-270f-52d1-ae19-fd266c2aef5d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c1cf14fc-3ea5-5845-8a1e-89cdf998a2cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-335237" :question/problem "For which of the following functions is it valid to differentiate under the integral sign?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as *differentiating under the integral sign.*\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each function:\n\n- For the first function, we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{1}(x,t)={t}^{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(tx).\n$$\n\nWe fix ${t}_{0}\\in R$ and choose $c<{t}_{0}<d,$ so $R=[0,1]\\times [c,d].$\n\nNote that ${f}_{1}$ is continuous on $R.$ Computing the partial derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂t}=2tx\\operatorname{cos}⁡(tx)-{t}^{2}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(tx)\n$$\n\nwhich exists and is continuous on $R.$ Thus, differentiating under the integral sign is valid at ${t}_{0}.$ And since our choice of ${t}_{0}$ was arbitrary, we can compute ${F}_{1}^{′}(t)$ for all real $t.$\n\n- For the second function, we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{2}(x,t)=\\frac{1}{(x-t)^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nWe fix ${t}_{0}\\in R$ and choose $c<{t}_{0}<d,$ so $R=[0,1]\\times [c,d].$\n\nNote that ${f}_{2}$ is continuous on $R$ because the denominator is always positive. Computing the partial derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂t}=\\frac{2(x-t)}{{((x-t)^{2}+1)}^{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich exists and is continuous on $R.$ Thus, differentiating under the integral sign is valid at ${t}_{0}.$ And since our choice of ${t}_{0}$ was arbitrary, we can compute ${F}_{2}^{′}(t)$ for all $t\\in R.$\n\n- For the third function, we have \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x,t)=\\frac{x}{x-t}.\n$$\n\nWe fix ${t}_{0}<0$ and choose $[c,d]⊂(-\\infty ,0)$ such that $c<{t}_{0}<d,$ so $R=[0,1]\\times [c,d].$\n\nNote that for $t<0$ and $x\\in [0,1],$ the denominator $x-t$ is positive, so ${f}_{3}$ is continuous on $R.$ Computing the partial derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂{f}_{3}}{∂t}=\\frac{x}{(x-t)^{2}}\n$$\n\nwhich exists and is continuous on $R.$ Thus, differentiating under the integral sign is valid at ${t}_{0}.$ And since our choice of ${t}_{0}$ was arbitrary, we can compute ${F}_{3}^{′}(t)$ for all $t<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${F}_{1}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(tx)\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\in R$; ${F}_{2}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{(x-t)^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t\\in R$; ${F}_{3}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{x}{x-t}\\,\\text{d}x,\\,t<0$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ab44ef0-82a0-5429-b0fc-9b1dab4f9d6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462309} {:answer/id #uuid "a25babc5-d215-54dc-ad9e-9e5ec99198ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a25babc5-d215-54dc-ad9e-9e5ec99198ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462310} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e56f8f7-d385-5fe6-852d-b65284d80e28" :answer-field/key "${D}_{1}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462908} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eda2342d-944d-52c9-abbf-40af297fa6fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462311} {:answer/id #uuid "6757bb8b-446e-5bcd-ab5a-35ba296407a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda2342d-944d-52c9-abbf-40af297fa6fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462311} :answer-field/id #uuid "5239be54-21a5-51be-85bf-f41d0402ad4e" :answer-field/key "${D}_{2}(y)={y}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462909} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "540ac414-b313-5137-a59a-c4005009519d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462313} {:answer/id #uuid "2c9213b2-edd3-5166-8011-d367453768b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462314}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "540ac414-b313-5137-a59a-c4005009519d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462313} :answer-field/id #uuid "da343601-ff70-5653-9dfe-edcf923521b1" :answer-field/key "${D}_{3}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-x\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462910} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dc0ce8d-2c4b-5e55-88bd-7805ecf824e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668020} {:answer/id #uuid "1dad16be-d310-5ca5-8175-4ee54df21368" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dc0ce8d-2c4b-5e55-88bd-7805ecf824e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668020} :answer-field/id #uuid "65d412e0-5db2-5e5d-95e5-8569604d0899" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668287}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fad9dda-1d37-5d53-a2df-c25ef4515a26" :question/math-academy-id "q-337662" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}=x,{f}_{1}=-2,$ and ${f}_{0}=0.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is ${y}^{2},$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The last term contains the nonlinear term ${y}^{2},$ which fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${D}_{1}(y)=x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "13e08fd0-4f41-56eb-8650-b72aa739b7a1" :knowledge-point/title "Initial Value Problems and Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "853427ec-ff39-510f-b5b9-b9b3063c4fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422189} {:answer/id #uuid "26f5c7b4-02a7-523d-971a-7bb512830680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f5c7b4-02a7-523d-971a-7bb512830680" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422190} :answer-field/id #uuid "f073f5b0-a749-5824-acf4-fa526c4e38fd" :answer-field/key "$(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422375} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2303430c-0704-550c-b6ae-374bc966f21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422191} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a09a9d-3bac-5120-8742-15c47fbf484c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2303430c-0704-550c-b6ae-374bc966f21d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422191} :answer-field/id #uuid "66f00add-7f80-5655-aba8-bf0b7b031d57" :answer-field/key "$8{y}^{′}-xy=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e36a2e5-c84a-5bb7-86bc-439a8b342c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422193} {:answer/id #uuid "707a477f-c377-547a-845c-170d00c19430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e36a2e5-c84a-5bb7-86bc-439a8b342c25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422193} :answer-field/id #uuid "e13181d5-74b1-59ab-977c-f7a710603e44" :answer-field/key "$3{y}^{″}$ $=4y,$ $\\,y(-1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(-1)$ $=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1f33eb7-98d6-5f89-b392-9bebcac6cd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667882} {:answer/id #uuid "8f40f981-4217-5018-942e-e6e618752836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1f33eb7-98d6-5f89-b392-9bebcac6cd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667882} :answer-field/id #uuid "ade126ad-e7f8-5345-a415-370ab36187dc" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668218}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7775ce93-f97a-564e-ab19-6ca38ffa6f3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-118786" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is a first-order initial value problem?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order initial value problem (or IVP) is a first-order ordinary differential equation together with an initial condition that specifies a value of the unknown function at a point in its domain. A first-order initial value problem typically takes the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y({x}_{0})={y}_{0},\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{0}$ and ${y}_{0}$ are constants.\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each option.\n\n- System $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$ is a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a first-order differential equation $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y$ together with the initial condition $y(-1)=3.$\n\n- System $8{y}^{′}-xy=3$ is not a first-order initial value problem. We have a first-order ordinary differential equation, but there is no initial condition.\n\n- System $3{y}^{″}$ $=4y,$ $\\,y(-1)$ $=0,$ $\\,{y}^{′}(-1)$ $=1$ is not a first-order initial value problem. It consists of a *second*-order differential equation $3{y}^{″}=4y$ together with *two* initial conditions $y(-1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(-1)=1.$ This is a second-order initial value problem.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $(1+{x}^{2}){y}^{′}=8y,\\,y(-1)=3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234490 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "443c0bd0-2e77-50a8-91d3-a288d4ee852b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Order of an Ordinary Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "6fddfc61-ae75-5f4b-8b2e-b3415ea0d369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408168} {:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "c834636a-bbd4-5759-b671-beb2e4da2abb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation I contains y'', so its highest derivative is second order." :answer/id #uuid "6fddfc61-ae75-5f4b-8b2e-b3415ea0d369" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408168} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f8bc9f-67ba-586b-b99e-1e38a930e19b" :answer-field/key "$3{y}^{''}+2x{y}^{'}={x}^{2}y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408169} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "df851142-894b-5bfb-8ece-98c5eb3b201e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408171} {:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "a4f9a0af-45e8-5e36-aa37-2b6d226dc143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation II contains y' and no higher derivative. The factor y^5 does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "a4f9a0af-45e8-5e36-aa37-2b6d226dc143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408173} :answer-field/id #uuid "22d9436b-ef55-5798-a20b-5e6bc9ca9430" :answer-field/key "$5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408172} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "1bb8cc3c-94ce-5d96-9edb-479fa67563b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408174} {:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "6e1d4c62-4dd2-5856-8d10-6a84849ff212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equation III contains y' and no higher derivative. The square root does not change the differential order." :answer/id #uuid "6e1d4c62-4dd2-5856-8d10-6a84849ff212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408176} :answer-field/id #uuid "495b552a-fc87-5ee2-b05d-892960260624" :answer-field/key "$\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Equations II and III are first-order ordinary differential equations." :answer/id #uuid "6a781e2b-45dc-581c-b89d-91bc1aa2c572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408177} {:answer/feedback "Equations II and III are first-order ordinary differential equations." :answer/id #uuid "451d2ac2-9a9b-5a8b-92c5-dbe6e540e9d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408179}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "Equations II and III are first-order ordinary differential equations." :answer/id #uuid "6a781e2b-45dc-581c-b89d-91bc1aa2c572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408177} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3890ce-bcc5-5fd3-810f-d1691316f3b1" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186408178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20db6c27-e8a9-50d0-bb54-61baf97c40e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96676" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order ordinary differential equations?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is of first-order if the largest derivative term in the equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nKeeping this in mind, let's check each given equation.\n\n- Equation $3{y}^{''}+2x{y}^{'}={x}^{2}y$ is not a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{''},$ so this is a second-order differential equation.\n\n- Equation $5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$ is a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\n- Equation $\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$ is also a first-order differential equation. The highest derivative in this equation is ${y}^{'}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $5{x}^{2}y+3{y}^{5}{y}^{'}=4x$; $\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+{y}^{'}}+7{x}^{3}={e}^{y}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237777 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66f7ea98-35bf-58a5-b5cf-b3254eac5084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461135} {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc959a-7ea6-5e88-b4be-f14a882c4c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bdc959a-7ea6-5e88-b4be-f14a882c4c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461136} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fc286e9-461c-5f4e-8e2a-ce7ca85ea019" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f16fb85-a3d0-575d-9438-1840969bac72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461137} {:answer/id #uuid "e99d91b1-b055-5c0f-823d-6d6ff3dec609" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f16fb85-a3d0-575d-9438-1840969bac72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461137} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee6e87c-88e4-5528-ba14-0dc349246406" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "628bdb8d-b415-5985-a3aa-cacb7f5d5e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461139} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea79588-ff3d-58b6-b8f1-64e70ed2b6b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "628bdb8d-b415-5985-a3aa-cacb7f5d5e03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461139} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd1bc0b4-9998-5eaf-aa5c-1bd1a6d60356" :answer-field/key "$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e752f41-73bb-5aea-919f-bb8254b1b367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667758} {:answer/id #uuid "05f691c9-8e9f-50c8-9387-0a6d17f7e546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667759}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e752f41-73bb-5aea-919f-bb8254b1b367" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667758} :answer-field/id #uuid "821ae51f-5ca9-5ad1-a9e2-e66e1e0f4583" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668156}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "68d1e936-89eb-56ca-bff3-c6afc2d2434a" :question/math-academy-id "q-100084" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2-2t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(1)q(1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,2-2t⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{1}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{1}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2-2t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)\\cdot (2-2(1))+(2-2)\\cdot (2-2(2)) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,2t⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{1}\\cdot (2t){|}_{1}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2t){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(1-2)\\cdot (2(1))+(2-2)\\cdot (2(2)) \\\\  & =-2\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0ef9b09-f091-52da-9498-81b25acbb057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461141} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c27c63-9782-5dca-8e3a-f89ed5ced033" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0ef9b09-f091-52da-9498-81b25acbb057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461141} :answer-field/id #uuid "481824b3-2e3f-592b-a547-b52518036348" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462324} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "440b28c8-ccdf-570c-94d8-a80cddfa6e92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461143} {:answer/id #uuid "07492636-38fb-5be2-a5fb-bc47855cd8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07492636-38fb-5be2-a5fb-bc47855cd8dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461144} :answer-field/id #uuid "281d9ea7-7201-5f95-8dee-0cc341703d58" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462325} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a65eb4c6-5adb-5c1e-ab17-ad96f89c6efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461145} {:answer/id #uuid "8fa75295-33ec-5de5-a6e8-187b0bb84398" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461146}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a65eb4c6-5adb-5c1e-ab17-ad96f89c6efe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461145} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d0c86fd-6c24-5d54-8ef6-ac2aaac69a47" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462326} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db825388-aae0-5a02-a7bf-74cd7e324a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667760} {:answer/id #uuid "05ac09fa-df9f-50f6-a322-ddf332dd4dd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db825388-aae0-5a02-a7bf-74cd7e324a10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667760} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a12ee77-b280-527e-a775-370df75d034b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668157}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "794f079c-000d-5b83-a34d-0c1430e5e296" :question/math-academy-id "q-100089" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t-1,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=1-t\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t-1,3t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t-1){|}_{0}\\cdot (3t){|}_{0}+(2t-1){|}_{1}\\cdot (3t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(2(0)-1)\\cdot (3(0))+(2(1)-1)\\cdot (3(1)) \\\\  & =3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,1-t⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{1}\\cdot (1-t){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(3(0))\\cdot (1-0)+(3(1))\\cdot (1-1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d0a68fa-7481-57f8-aac8-231b6d17e53c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461147} {:answer/id #uuid "d32374fd-da40-5f0b-9123-a100afc15f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461148}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d32374fd-da40-5f0b-9123-a100afc15f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461148} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5f57b84-47a1-52ef-9389-ed82a67a5278" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462327} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fcf97229-8208-5030-b620-6bfcaa175228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461149} {:answer/id #uuid "97ebaddc-b05e-55da-b8ee-a57a63b5dd44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461150}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcf97229-8208-5030-b620-6bfcaa175228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461149} :answer-field/id #