lty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e68e3d26-aa65-5eb7-b898-7c00e9b7271e" :question/math-academy-id "q-100091" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-1,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-1)q(-1)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-1,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(t-1){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(t-1){|}_{1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-1-1)\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(1-1)\\cdot (1+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is false since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨2,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(2){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1}+(2){|}_{1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(2)\\cdot ((-1)+1)+(2)\\cdot (1+1) \\\\  & =4\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237781 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db20fdb5-b211-5717-8065-e53a2737e52f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461153} {:answer/id #uuid "6656a7b8-c8ea-5900-b91f-827cf9160375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461154}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6656a7b8-c8ea-5900-b91f-827cf9160375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461154} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e43ba6a-40ab-5c1a-b8c8-a8858483f612" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20ed73bc-5b6f-5ab3-960f-9b7f15c8d785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461155} {:answer/id #uuid "9793f44e-45c4-5a51-9746-6e6a99a83a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9793f44e-45c4-5a51-9746-6e6a99a83a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461156} :answer-field/id #uuid "ded516f2-2e1d-5b1d-9ede-938fe1e44d44" :answer-field/key "${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb2b82bd-c25b-51f4-bfaf-3cdcb7a1a58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461157} {:answer/id #uuid "3b12847b-cc3a-5250-b4d9-33f8b9d8c07f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461158}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb2b82bd-c25b-51f4-bfaf-3cdcb7a1a58f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461157} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb5c838-cff5-5fc9-b5c7-6f2cc94f2a50" :answer-field/key "$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462332} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "068d612c-5dbf-53af-ac45-2bfbf6ae1a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667764} {:answer/id #uuid "1ff08a4f-7c3f-5ac3-acdc-1bb73804aabe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "068d612c-5dbf-53af-ac45-2bfbf6ae1a2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667764} :answer-field/id #uuid "77968d17-2331-54f3-b03b-2df70eb8417d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea1a91d4-93f7-5e8d-b2ce-c7694a823cec" :question/math-academy-id "q-100114" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+1,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=3t,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(-1)q(-1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨2t+1,3t⟩ \\\\  & =(2t+1){|}_{0}\\cdot (3t){|}_{0}+(2t+1){|}_{-1}\\cdot (3t){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =(2(0)+1)\\cdot (3(0))+(2(-1)+1)\\cdot (3(-1)) \\\\  & =3\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨3t,t+1⟩ \\\\  & =(3t){|}_{0}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{0}+(3t){|}_{-1}\\cdot (t+1){|}_{-1} \\\\  & =(3(0))\\cdot (0+1)+(3(-1))\\cdot ((-1)+1) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Since ${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t),$ the set $S$ is *not* orthogonal.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥̸{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2bcfcb6-8f8b-5aa9-8346-05db880fa5bb" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Set of Polynomials is Orthogonal With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4bc79c40-802c-5928-96bd-62b5abc8ad53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461159} {:answer/id #uuid "624f3dda-272a-59f4-81c4-afdc89b1b569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "624f3dda-272a-59f4-81c4-afdc89b1b569" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461160} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1795204-45a0-5ae2-b1e0-fe24f1661e9a" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462333} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d409008c-3927-5c03-9206-ddde6c3ce4c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461161} {:answer/id #uuid "1a4f7f7d-e705-5bea-b85e-15ecc20591e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a4f7f7d-e705-5bea-b85e-15ecc20591e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461162} :answer-field/id #uuid "75ba454e-4199-5bbb-a3a5-a8496e22c83d" :answer-field/key "${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462334} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10ce821b-8ac0-57db-b8d9-ccfbcbc7d8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461163} {:answer/id #uuid "3128022b-3800-59d4-aea7-1dbf26659f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461164}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10ce821b-8ac0-57db-b8d9-ccfbcbc7d8fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461163} :answer-field/id #uuid "104242d5-dc4e-5e24-ac69-a557c354d5fa" :answer-field/key "$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462335} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73a45b24-d709-5083-9b4a-5030c83e556d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667766} {:answer/id #uuid "9483b867-745f-5349-8e39-0fb309173dbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667767}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73a45b24-d709-5083-9b4a-5030c83e556d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667766} :answer-field/id #uuid "a6542b07-d00a-5551-86a3-cdd0672cf50e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0e262e4d-a912-58d1-aa39-b29d3810a43d" :question/math-academy-id "q-100119" :question/problem "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=2t+4.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(-2)q(-2)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,t+2⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{-2}\\cdot (t+2){|}_{-2}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (t+2){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(-2-2)\\cdot ((-2)+2)+(2-2)\\cdot (2+2) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” is true. Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t-2,2t+4⟩ \\\\  & =(t-2){|}_{-2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{-2}+(t-2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{2} \\\\  & =(-2-2)\\cdot (2(-2)+4)+(2-2)\\cdot (2(2)+4) \\\\  & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product.\n\n- Statement “$S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product” is false. Let's check if ${p}_{2}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t).$ Computing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)⟩ & =⟨t+2,2t+4⟩ \\\\  & =(t+2){|}_{-2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{-2}+(t+2){|}_{2}\\cdot (2t+4){|}_{2} \\\\  & =((-2)+2)\\cdot (2(-2)+4)+(2+2)\\cdot (2(2)+4) \\\\  & =32\\ne 0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that ${p}_{2}(t)⊥̸{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product. So, the set $S$ is *not* an orthogonal set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product”; “${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237797 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147492 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e71c0c9-7dd1-5f09-a55c-96b5bed1ee9a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Differential Equation Corresponding to a Phase Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49ec8218-3450-52de-b41b-a093639721ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461165} {:answer/id #uuid "921a73f8-3ee7-59fd-81bc-c93a9d997217" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49ec8218-3450-52de-b41b-a093639721ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461165} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cc424b5-73f5-5e6a-9116-73ba780ee733" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462336} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27885c74-a274-5c78-94e8-5552f9a71fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461167} {:answer/id #uuid "b099c22f-e7a7-5176-bfb9-76577a381d83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27885c74-a274-5c78-94e8-5552f9a71fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461167} :answer-field/id #uuid "dedb7b4e-aa3c-5664-9589-a46141092606" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}-y$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf4cc38e-88b9-5451-bf44-deba8b4ed1ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461169} {:answer/id #uuid "7ac205dd-a5bd-5d74-b4fd-b5f71d11d811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461170}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ac205dd-a5bd-5d74-b4fd-b5f71d11d811" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461170} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b40d879-9d0e-596b-8019-dd8be3a85185" :answer-field/key "$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)(y-2)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eda1932f-fbcd-50e8-9907-a9831292833f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667770} {:answer/id #uuid "4a371699-4e84-5fae-b567-ab75820ca042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667771}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda1932f-fbcd-50e8-9907-a9831292833f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667770} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7258040-f9d3-5f33-8b23-2b1b93b3062a" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "74569aa4-36e3-5e4d-99a5-eeb148ed4156" :question/math-academy-id "q-100569" :question/problem "![](images/37/375647b4e2527841b48da5405effe2f15502f1d972586556796a55bcff441b94.png)\n\nConsider the phase line shown above. Which of the following differential equations could have this phase line?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all three differential equations are of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThe phase line gives us the following information:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=-1,$ $y=0$ and $y=2.$\n\n- $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (0,2).$\n\n- $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (-1,0)\\cup (2,\\infty ).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's study each of the given equations.\n\n- We start by considering ${y}^{′}=-y(y+1)^{2}.$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=-y(y+1)^{2},$ and the equilibrium solutions are $y=-1,0$ only. \n\nTherefore, equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)^{2}$ does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Next, we consider ${y}^{′}={y}^{3}-y.$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=y(y-1)(y+1),$ and the equilibrium solutions are $y=-1,0,1$ only. \n\nTherefore, equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={y}^{3}-y$ does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Finally, we consider ${y}^{′}=-y(y+1)(y-2).$\n\nFirst, we see that $f(y)=-y(y+1)(y-2),$ so $f(y)=0$ if $y=-1,0,2.$ So, the equilibrium solutions correspond to those shown in the phase line.\n\nNow, we can construct a sign table for $f(y)$ as follows: \n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,-1)$ | $(-1,0)$ | $(0,2)$ | $(2,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y+1$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $-y$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| $y-2$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (-1,0)\\cup (2,\\infty ),$ and $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (0,2).$ This corresponds to the arrows shown on the phase line.\n\nTherefore, equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)(y-2)$ has the given phase line.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-y(y+1)(y-2)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237862 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115380 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "794398c0-ffbf-5971-a411-f236607f56b8" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function is Differentiable at a Point Given a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ad7ef9d-6acc-5ee0-8cbe-2c445ee6e375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461189} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe63e74-5a8d-583d-a073-d909903628bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461190}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ad7ef9d-6acc-5ee0-8cbe-2c445ee6e375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461189} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9af70e7-f63b-580d-9382-7998be071336" :answer-field/key "The function is continuous at $x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462348} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a1f9aea-858f-500c-acda-7a508c9ffa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461191} {:answer/id #uuid "d3695edf-ea67-5c61-8197-e2046d6d8849" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a1f9aea-858f-500c-acda-7a508c9ffa0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461191} :answer-field/id #uuid "507608ea-131d-5566-943f-d6991e34b29f" :answer-field/key "The function is differentiable at $x=-5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462349} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fc7f3bc-6079-5131-be86-1662d3ec264a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461193} {:answer/id #uuid "57c7df08-a8c0-585f-9280-89506d78dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461194}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57c7df08-a8c0-585f-9280-89506d78dee6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461194} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d2276e8-6e00-56fc-98dd-dbbff77f2df5" :answer-field/key "The function is differentiable at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462350} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be4e535c-5cd2-5d2d-971c-0561056a6089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667772} {:answer/id #uuid "1c194660-f747-5270-ad6b-a677b76e2503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be4e535c-5cd2-5d2d-971c-0561056a6089" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667772} :answer-field/id #uuid "93e4514d-699f-5efc-8386-b47299a7e71b" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08a8dbc9-b97f-57b3-acad-4c86f2f3f516" :question/math-academy-id "q-101983" :question/problem "![](images/dc/dc27a54ac20efc84bfbc404a20a91309c60c3fb42118f164129e93eee584437b.png)\n\nGiven the plot of the function $y=f(x)$ above, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=-5$” is false. The function has an infinite discontinuity at $x=-5.$\n\n- Statement “The function is differentiable at $x=-5$” is false. Since $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-5$ it can't be differentiable there either.\n\n- Statement “The function is differentiable at $x=0$” is true. The function is continuous at $x=0$ and doesn't have a corner point, a  cusp, or a vertical tangent.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The function is differentiable at $x=0$”  is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "512f4d7d-a50e-5ac1-9b00-a23a2f1e85a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461195} {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1be740a2-c20f-5fc9-8ec8-1f106667add1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461196} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3434df-a85b-5891-9fca-5190f4d5b98e" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462351} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50a3ad9b-e804-5cca-a228-07b5c0f5b67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461197} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd91feb-5abf-5ad2-b1f4-c8b98678090d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50a3ad9b-e804-5cca-a228-07b5c0f5b67f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461197} :answer-field/id #uuid "09fa150b-0bcd-5369-b4b9-9a606723ef7f" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc30d3d1-1efe-582e-944c-8f9d386f5738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461199} {:answer/id #uuid "2dd1d8db-a0f8-5a3f-9666-d01d5c0ea372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc30d3d1-1efe-582e-944c-8f9d386f5738" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461199} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9afc227-2585-54bd-9518-4d409658168b" :answer-field/key "$C={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462353} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8b74bf6-a621-5308-98a0-14238c348767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667774} {:answer/id #uuid "464ad2b8-ee52-5022-93f2-b63be11b3301" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8b74bf6-a621-5308-98a0-14238c348767" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667774} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd5f8d98-5204-57cb-a685-d86ceb24939d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668164}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "efd9ac2b-7a32-57f6-9899-3da1aeffaa13" :question/math-academy-id "q-102666" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $C={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3743095-b86d-5690-811f-9531139d1e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461201} {:answer/id #uuid "0ac7323d-