 above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "67a1c719-c84d-5d17-9d41-c30fb7529952" :question/math-academy-id "q-102670" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AB=BA={I}_{2}$; $C\\ne {A}^{-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237921 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields