 #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667786} {:answer/id #uuid "f781cc61-aa59-558e-86cb-b30625f9a164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f781cc61-aa59-558e-86cb-b30625f9a164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667787} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b271cae-052f-501a-8146-56e94422011d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "21ccde81-8669-5255-b2ed-8bdddd923bd6" :question/math-academy-id "q-103152" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x-5)^{n}$ converges at  $x=2,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=5,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=2,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $3,$ i.e., $R\\ge 3.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $[2,8).$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $[2,8).$\n\n![](images/df/dfd59d22892764c4da387d48b07a6a1069ea59e13be75cd099d21ce53975d64c.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series diverges at $x=6$” is false. Since $6\\in [2,8),$ the series is convergent at $x=6.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=0$” is false. Since $0\\notin [2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=8$” is false. Since $8\\notin [2,8),$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the listed.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237977 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175956 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60f61c26-ff2d-5343-becd-d8f44f623cd3" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Convergence of a Power Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbe55739-eaf9-56ed-9d81-8e52c2ca8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461249} {:answer/id #uuid "529614bd-8f87-5f2c-80b4-5c37e138c066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbe55739-eaf9-56ed-9d81-8e52c2ca8a75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461249} :answer-field/id #uuid "c392bd2e-f2f9-5ceb-b0b1-f3a1b122ab52" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-11$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462378} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c50d44-335d-5651-ba10-b49f0f37fe9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461251} {:answer/id #uuid "61ae86b3-caf9-536d-bef5-f22c8cc87cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461252}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61ae86b3-caf9-536d-bef5-f22c8cc87cac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461252} :answer-field/id #uuid "ce112048-db7b-58d9-ac72-bb8feec404bb" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=-8$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} {:answer/id #uuid "ace51aeb-e1da-564d-aaa1-10285b642108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26ec3d05-89ca-5e41-af7d-d0230d5cab2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461253} :answer-field/id #uuid "72accc2e-3370-511e-9b00-a598c293557b" :answer-field/key "The series converges at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aaaadf5b-2c98-5029-8e2e-d1169a836cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667788} {:answer/id #uuid "19b15084-e4f8-56a8-8c77-55741be7b477" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667789}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aaaadf5b-2c98-5029-8e2e-d1169a836cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667788} :answer-field/id #uuid "15a870d6-1d58-50bf-943b-105d524aa80d" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668171}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "76850d0b-0e5d-5926-80f5-97253aff4b0d" :question/math-academy-id "q-103170" :question/problem "Given that the power series ${\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(x+7)^{n}$ converges at  $x=-3,$ which of the following **must** be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The center of the expansion is $x=-7,$ and since the series is convergent for $x=-3,$ this means that the radius of convergence $R$ is *at least* $4,$ i.e., $R\\ge 4.$ So, the series is convergent for every point in the interval $(-11,-3].$ However, we know nothing about the convergence of the series at any point outside the interval $(-11,-3].$\n\n![](images/47/4764256e5f00e7a11d688bd99d5fa1c22db819e7a188113f0ef4cd987a9b7595.png)\n\n \n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of our statements.\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-11$” is false. Since $-11\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=-11.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=-8$” is true. Since $-8\\in (-11,-3],$ the series is convergent at $x=-8.$\n\n- Statement “The series converges at $x=1$” is false. Since $1\\notin (-11,-3],$ we cannot guarantee that the series is convergent at $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The series converges at $x=-8$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064162 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a595bc07-ad64-537d-be42-06144814b97d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Extrema of a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b293e62f-6f87-5e32-9d47-30001e75a473" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461279} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a8359a-378f-5d30-b9c0-f8c4d4fb9c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461280}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2a8359a-378f-5d30-b9c0-f8c4d4fb9c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461280} :answer-field/id #uuid "92f57ac4-00e1-5c7e-9979-b50b20bf610f" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462393} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f6cc80e1-8c2d-50ca-9f1e-11ffa91bfdf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461281} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3f2ac5-9e21-5c73-81bb-3e709f16ae1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461282}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d3f2ac5-9e21-5c73-81bb-3e709f16ae1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461282} :answer-field/id #uuid "71c3c88f-d59c-59fa-bfdc-8de1c22722c3" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a4c59c3-0fa7-57fd-a77c-691d443f258c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461283} {:answer/id #uuid "9d12003a-0d3f-510e-b2aa-cfbebcab6a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461284}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d12003a-0d3f-510e-b2aa-cfbebcab6a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461284} :answer-field/id #uuid "37ed8c1c-74af-5b75-8c3b-0d241ae04ccb" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462395} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e79b52d0-6b85-5411-84b7-5e56627db8e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667790} {:answer/id #uuid "08626077-4fca-5190-9a51-42877d898a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e79b52d0-6b85-5411-84b7-5e56627db8e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667790} :answer-field/id #uuid "b7efb14b-9f7d-5dfb-a0ce-9c62921da47e" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a2c02942-de68-547a-8bfa-7932a2f390a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-103438" :question/problem "![](images/5b/5bbb0cacbe8dca2facfd49e757ba9b7aa40ee91ae820f001c72d637186d57b79.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our statements.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a critical point at $x=-1$” is true. The function has a critical point (a corner) at $x=-1.$ In this case,  ${f}^{′}(-1)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a stationary point at $x=0$” is true. Stationary points are points where ${f}^{′}(x)=0.$ In this case, the graph of the function has a horizontal tangent line at $x=0,$ and therefore, ${f}^{′}(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$f(x)$ has a local minimum at $x=1$” is true. The function has a local minimum at $x=1$ since $f(1)\\le f(x)$ for all $x$ close enough to $x=1.$\n\nTherefore, all three statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48f0646c-449a-55f7-a43e-10aed917f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461285} {:answer/id #uuid "6f47c9f4-cfdf-51cc-a8ee-2e312b6e2ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48f0646c-449a-55f7-a43e-10aed917f0d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461285} :answer-field/id #uuid "e42517c5-86d0-573b-9c42-a43146a898c4" :answer-field/key "The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462396} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be579ceb-8f73-508e-8274-146cdc8bb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461287} {:answer/id #uuid "19f14dea-5bfb-587c-9cb9-670c75f65f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be579ceb-8f73-508e-8274-146cdc8bb7b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461287} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac105e7-89d8-52b0-b5e6-9803aa72f310" :answer-field/key "The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fbd3708f-69c6-5fb0-a0c2-d6332aefe29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461289} {:answer/id #uuid "5df81d82-6062-53b0-8ac4-34d404968f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbd3708f-69c6-5fb0-a0c2-d6332aefe29b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461289} :answer-field/id #uuid "4deab2df-6f34-5f4c-8d22-c93a07225cea" :answer-field/key "The function is continuous at $x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462398} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8b22fff-40cd-5e6f-8cec-9c60503af7a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667792} {:answer/id #uuid "da289da4-af8c-5bd5-9aad-e1b5447b6ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da289da4-af8c-5bd5-9aad-e1b5447b6ecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667793} :answer-field/id #uuid "893c6e42-4b90-5359-a0bf-17543e2d6e79" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668173}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d00cc33e-d21d-57ae-828a-16fa83891b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-104357" :question/problem "![](images/30/30df82b4c47905fd8277067f9207a5e970a96d8ec386879d2872b5f5c3d8dd3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=f(x)$ plotted above?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “The function is left-continuous at $x=-1$” is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{-}}f(x)=1\\ne 0=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is right-continuous at $x=-1$” is false. The function is not right-continuous at $x=-1,$ since the right-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-1)^{+}}f(x)=-1\\ne 0=f(-1)\n$$\n\n- Statement “The function is continuous at $x=-1$” is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=-1,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is neither left-continuous nor right-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240899 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129086 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9110c50a-62db-5447-b4d0-60819c80eb31" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties Related to Point Discontinuities Given a Function Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58795638-a192-5cb2-add6-072256161aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461297} {:answer/id #uuid "f8618f49-d2bc-5685-9c55-7c8a9a585828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461298}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8618f49-d2bc-5685-9c55-7c8a9a585828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461298} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0bfa1fe-ca62-5b36-b004-861e91cb01da" :answer-field/key "${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)$ $={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462402} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7b4c029-937e-5c36-8214-90b1d5fad103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref