592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667796} :answer-field/id #uuid "f216ae3a-fe13-5dc9-b19a-d9cc41e2fffb" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7bdde4d8-daa6-55ef-bcc6-21f99b29d77c" :question/math-academy-id "q-104575" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}g(x) & ={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-34, & x<-3 \\\\ -25, & x=-3 \\\\ {x}^{3}+2, & x>-3\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's check our continuity conditions:\n\n- $g(-3)=-25$ exists $\\,✓$\n\n- The left and right-sided limits are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{-}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{-}}({x}^{2}-34)=(-3)^{2}-34=-25, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}g(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to \\,(-3)^{+}}({x}^{3}+2)=(-3)^{3}+2=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are equal, we conclude that statement ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)$ $={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=-25.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- The value of the limit is ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=-25,$ and the value of the function is $g(-3)=-25.$ So, statement ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)$ is true and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, the function is continuous at $x=-3,$ and statement “$g(x)$ has a removable discontinuity at $x=-3$” is false.\n\nIn conclusion, only statements ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}g(x)$ $={lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}g(x)$ and ${lim}_{x\\to (-3)}g(x)=g(-3)$ are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054815 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abc6b3ee-0251-5c9c-9358-bd192c434dd1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Elements Belonging to Scripted 