nswer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "584b6ea8-930f-5b89-94ba-983ab55cd684" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461495} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec95b7a8-1630-5830-acd6-e28d5986273c" :answer-field/key "$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aef0e7af-93b7-5531-809e-2739874c6809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667814} {:answer/id #uuid "98278eef-5c07-5da6-8278-6dd4517338a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667815}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98278eef-5c07-5da6-8278-6dd4517338a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667815} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c0c1f94-476c-5bcb-83e5-4664ca8bd7dd" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fba7ca1e-918b-5610-87e4-9553b3a87d7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107589" :question/problem "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ and $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$” is false. Since $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$, any vector of ${R}^{2},$ including the given vector $x,$ can be written as a linear combination of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ This means that $\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x\\}$ is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$” is false. The set $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the vector ${b}_{3}$ is in ${R}^{3}$ but it is not a linear combination of  ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ as the set  $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent. This means that the set does not span ${R}^{3}$ and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement “$\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$” is false. The set $\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{c}_{1}\\}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244144 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4149ef3f-74da-5a1a-9c28-c1d8593e3ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437526} {:answer/id #uuid "f842b5cb-cf9f-52db-975f-f671411d8fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4149ef3f-74da-5a1a-9c28-c1d8593e3ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1