da =2$ of $A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462543} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49f7a71d-1363-54e5-942c-cdaea0b5a5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667840} {:answer/id #uuid "e9ef755b-7c28-504b-8651-91e18f72c9e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667841}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49f7a71d-1363-54e5-942c-cdaea0b5a5a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667840} :answer-field/id #uuid "89d81498-36c3-52ce-a5f4-43c75f0b65c8" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a65ad08d-f6cf-551f-aa17-5ecb903998d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-109524" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A-2I:$\n\n$$\nA-2I=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-2I:$\n\n$$\n(A-2I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{v}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\overset{A-2I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-2I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is “$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ of $A$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76e60bc4-ae61-5c39-ad80-14e0cdab14da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Generalized Eigenvectors of a 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b486bce2-fa4e-513e-b610-7ee71b9233d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461581} {:answer/id #uuid "c967c74a-a0ee-5cb2-add3-5fb704306c38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461582}] :answer-field/c