ef 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "73154a72-4618-59f1-ab95-d4b82ca2da71" :question/math-academy-id "q-109632" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,v=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ and vector $v$ shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A-3I:$\n\n$$\nA-3I=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-3I:$\n\n$$\n(A-3I)v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-3I:$\n\n$$\n(A-3I)w=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A-3I:$\n\n$$\n(A-3I)x=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{v}\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}_{w}\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}_{x}\\overset{A-3I\\,}{\\to }\\underbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-3I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247149 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ad39641-56c0-508c-9b90-0cc2e2767b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461641} {:answer/id #uuid "02252817-c38b-5820-b87f-ed1696a4c751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ad39641-56c0-508c-9b90-0cc2e2767b7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461641} :answer-field/id #uuid "857885bf-7367-5e75-8ec5-43d94868cb82" :answer-field/key "![Diagram I](images/43/435ae803182d813230907411b7104b5239d287d294ec69f5d1a0a4112258518a.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462574} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73f09b04-09ec-5e1f-bdf5-e3178c28f434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461643} {:answer/id #uuid "01faef8b-4f0b-51b2-80ff-1f9d1ade44d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73f09b04-09ec-5e1f-bdf5-e3178c28f434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461643} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5d5341b-98e6-512b-8142-c17dfa8068d4" :answer-field/key "![Diagram II](images/54/541aa5367d8bb8bd36ea5811579728513153549aa66066d491357f43c5aad11d.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462575} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c52a9d4d-a545-519c-8a5a-0c045175f03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461645} {:answer/id #uuid "15b5b644-7d14-50d4-8d39-f862963ee03f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c52a9d4d-a545-519c-8a5a-0c045175f03a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461645} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ac97ed8-0d07-5bff-b5b5-97985053e7bd" :answer-field/key "![Diagram III](images/84/8480765d37746d4157a336140609e46919f93ceba05aaed2c595cca8c1e1ccb0.svg)" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462576} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153dd84c-6d2a-536b-9c6e-28308cea6f80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667858} {:answer/id #uuid "c2e322ae-5573-5b99-9991-25ffc95df55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c2e322ae-5573-5b99-9991-25ffc95df55c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667859} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb18c004-09bf-5415-983e-819c0b6ff7d0" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668206}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3f37be5a-fb02-59a0-9bc3-1e609a53d6d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-110600" :question/problem "Which of the diagrams shown below represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace. The vector $a=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ lies inside the given subset. But \n\n$$\n(-1)\\cdot a=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nlies outside the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a set that does not contain the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram II is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$ without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247290 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6ed7dd8-66bc-5071-a37b-951be908d6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437552} {:answer/id #uuid "704578a1-0e4a-595b-92eb-eb054da1a896" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6ed7dd8-66bc-5071-a37b-951be908d6c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437552} :answer-field/id #uuid "84f102cd-f012-58fa-bb1e-aaba22574b2c" :answer-field/key "$p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438805} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78ae4065-0902-5d39-8e60-d94c4d044941" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437554} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e1e703-3563-57e8-a33b-c4d461d13f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4e1e703-3563-57e8-a33b-c4d461d13f44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437555} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bb599a0-7b6d-5eda-b1cc-1490ff53bccb" :answer-field/key "$p(0)=0.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438806} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc7e2bcb-12bd-5d36-961b-0822cf128846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437556} {:answer/id #uuid "007486f7-f7cb-5355-b8c3-7905fd60e0cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc7e2bcb-12bd-5d36-961b-0822cf128846" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437556} :answer-field/id #uuid "06fc1b00-0e36-5e62-acd3-5be7dc024152" :answer-field/key "$x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438807} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47ce611c-6a98-5925-afa3-a11a5ccbc9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667860} {:answer/id #uuid "6f34c1d5-ff25-503f-b948-d350e36e80e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667861}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47ce611c-6a98-5925-afa3-a11a5ccbc9c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667860} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e72ffa-753c-59da-984b-a595e4154b77" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "576d8616-a0cd-59d9-a961-712779c4c308" :question/math-academy-id "q-112587" :question/problem "![](images/aa/aa431232a1f9ef2374f4e8a9c0202cf60ce1dcfef69c2a6fca604fe6aed7b681.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$p(x)\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to -\\infty .$” is false. As $x$ moves left in the negative direction towards $-\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement $p(0)=0.$ is true. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=0$, which means that $p(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity” is false. The root $x=1$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $p(0)=0.$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors When the Denominator Has Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb9d7b25-5854-520d-8ebf-a6801866a103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439439} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd9b49f-1e1e-558e-9235-e08d3e02c10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9d7b25-5854-520d-8ebf-a6801866a103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439439} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9087893-bc60-52fc-8d81-3cedf3411ac6" :answer-field/key "$x=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ddf72a-287c-5883-9635-ec2b9399d667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439441} {:answer/id #uuid "59344e22-da7e-5c4e-9b1f-2a9bd6abb444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ddf72a-287c-5883-9635-ec2b9399d667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439441} :answer-field/id #uuid "a46f02c4-4697-588e-bc3e-a16a5e0bec49" :answer-field/key "$x=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044decdf-112a-5933-b2b2-02be3db90f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439443} {:answer/id #uuid "91341243-61ec-5cbb-8cb0-aa4b45e28585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "044decdf-112a-5933-b2b2-02be3db90f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439443} :answer-field/id #uuid "f27daf57-7ce5-534a-ba37-ad6313ed2cc9" :answer-field/key "$x=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8cf81f43-7491-5a14-8e73-b1427991975f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667862} {:answer/id #uuid "3ca976cd-1494-58af-bd0e-b728c49a3dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667863}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3ca976cd-1494-58af-bd0e-b728c49a3dae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667863} :answer-field/id #uuid "f510af0b-435d-5acb-97fc-4f3725ed169c" :answer-field/key "The function has no vertical asymptotes" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668208}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "daec1f65-9c08-5df4-939b-bebb2395a749" :question/math-academy-id "q-113545" :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}+x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =1-4(1)(2) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250218 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184151 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "437c168a-6799-5d13-bd9b-031290a84da6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intervals of Concavity of a Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16429656-5c03-5aa3-aaf3-aa7d1ebeed61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461683} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c0d93b-dc86-5e59-8c16-ccc5da156329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16429656-5c03-5aa3-aaf3-aa7d1ebeed61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186461683} :answer-field/id #uuid "c796127d-850a-53b5-b48c-1f585671fed2" :answer-field/key "$f(x)$ is concave down on $(1,\\infty )$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186462595} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12f3546f-2758-5f53-a269-4d4aac9e177f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1