ative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$∇f$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $∇f$ is conservative by definition.\n\n- Statement “${∮}_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any piecewise linear path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” is false. The result $Γ=0$ applies to closed curves only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$∇f$ is conservative” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259842 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179743 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1da220a9-2afc-5b63-a423-a4d2b3de9567" :knowledge-point/title "Circulation in Conservative Vector Fields"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09c4ca32-01d3-5738-bf72-b8352d5c52bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463518} {:answer/id #uuid "da99aeb6-90d2-5e8f-b5d8-7b05292fda87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "da99aeb6-90d2-5e8f-b5d8-7b05292fda87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463519} :answer-field/id #uuid "919615d2-0f76-58af-8761-3a14fe46d18f" :answer-field/key "$F$ is conservative" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d9db93-5a15-5b46-8273-d519f8d86e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463520} {:answer/id #uuid "2539dad8-dc80-5397-b9a8-c578eeb0666a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2539dad8-dc80-5397-b9a8-c578eeb0666a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463521} :answer-field/id #uuid "60cccf49-fa44-52b6-860d-b7a17aa98cbe" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e642cf7-9d5f-5e17-8e6f-08394c3a7be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463522} {:answer/id #uuid "f50da4f3-efa9-5c80-b985-c77c0571181a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f50da4f3-efa9-5c80-b985-c77c0571181a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463523} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa9dff9-ff4d-597d-8ef9-69284d5d1e3f" :answer-field/key "${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464695} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69d3df83-92d2-5184-b675-b6a5c3c18aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667922} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6cf91a-81b7-5496-9df1-104d1cfe81a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69d3df83-92d2-5184-b675-b6a5c3c18aac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667922} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d1a290b-e2a2-5929-b0ab-5562df71eb45" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2353653c-eb1d-5d31-b3c0-eed1015199de" :question/math-academy-id "q-125664" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=({y}^{2}+3x)\\,i+(2xy+3)\\,j.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If $F$ is a conservative vector field on ${R}^{2},$ then the circulation $Γ=0$ for any *closed* path $C\\in {R}^{2},$ that is \n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\nWe notice that $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with domain $D={R}^{2}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=2y.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement “$F$ is conservative” is true. The vector field $F$ is conservative since the partial derivatives are equal and continuous everywhere on ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Statement “${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$” and “${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$” are true. The circulation $Γ=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$F$ is conservative”; “${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any circle $C\\in {R}^{2}$”; “${∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$ for any closed path $C\\in {R}^{2}$”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087696 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3ca13445-0218-5950-967e-a68bcfec32c7" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Square Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe5658b2-ecbf-5729-a03d-3906b20cccbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463580} {:answer/id #uuid "21c517ff-d927-5410-8a65-4207f1706ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463581}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "21c517ff-d927-5410-8a65-4207f1706ec6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463581} :answer-field/id #uuid "e80c3713-3550-5c60-bf0c-0821c17d963c" :answer-field/key "$K=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464724} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7f323ab-c5d9-5fff-aecb-db53cbab4e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463582} {:answer/id #uuid "1560c66f-7a1a-5947-9f60-03688b1f8b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7f323ab-c5d9-5fff-aecb-db53cbab4e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463582} :answer-field/id #uuid "7be7bbda-907a-5513-a354-940218369f61" :answer-field/key "$L=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3730365-1faa-567b-9c31-4acdc410ed4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463584} {:answer/id #uuid "869dcee3-6d63-5587-84d7-2a86bd969317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3730365-1faa-567b-9c31-4acdc410ed4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463584} :answer-field/id #uuid "3622dfcc-ed36-50f5-8709-40aff4162d7a" :answer-field/key "$M=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464726} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cc64ec95-0d0c-536b-85dc-51a200431fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667924} {:answer/id #uuid "84a5cfeb-19f2-57db-803d-12d9c5c0047e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc64ec95-0d0c-536b-85dc-51a200431fea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667924} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1e9d840-7ea4-5439-8a33-655fd0261565" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0dc57098-3c69-5567-91db-1d90d4ec9c40" :question/math-academy-id "q-126275" :question/problem "Which of the following are square matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $K$ is a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. It has $2$ rows and $2$ columns, so it is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $L$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $1$ rows and $2$ columns, so it's a $1\\times 2$ matrix.\n\n- $M$ is *not* a square matrix since the numbers of rows and columns are not the same. It has $4$ rows and $3$ columns, so it's a $4\\times 3$ matrix.\n\nTherefore, only $K$ is a square matrix."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064280 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5b4b32f9-8362-5c81-a1fe-4457d91ae571" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Functions That Satisfy the Mean Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8424311-5774-5664-af5d-dfb6a6dc0336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463592} {:answer/id #uuid "e73779e5-1d0f-59d8-a3a1-18ac78c7b845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e73779e5-1d0f-59d8-a3a1-18ac78c7b845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463593} :answer-field/id #uuid "46749a79-894a-5c79-8d45-eb84e3aa3d82" :answer-field/key "$p(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464730} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58abab50-c2c8-5df3-b217-1f786f9653b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463594} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c2d4d5-6b1d-5ea5-9ab9-a9533b8b0ea5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463595}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58abab50-c2c8-5df3-b217-1f786f9653b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463594} :answer-field/id #uuid "110ee671-4220-5bb9-afb8-70a255ce921c" :answer-field/key "$q(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464731} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f37d08d2-b69c-5300-928b-c280ca4f7e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463596} {:answer/id #uuid "43f857e8-d7b2-59b9-97d9-8a8843875c4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f37d08d2-b69c-5300-928b-c280ca4f7e97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463596} :answer-field/id #uuid "4887ee96-65c2-57c9-bbb3-1d2d022f0460" :answer-field/key "$r(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(|x-1|)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464732} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd0148b5-b152-51af-974c-a7ffca301f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667926} {:answer/id #uuid "13219673-bf59-5e06-b215-e3bd6f24edd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd0148b5-b152-51af-974c-a7ffca301f79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667926} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c4cb8cd-479c-5553-99d6-75faaee03f53" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b52094f1-1c52-540b-aa05-57b1e1d10dfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-127014" :question/problem "Which of the following functions satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3]?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function to satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3],$ the function must be continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$\n\nLet's check each function individually.\n\n- The function $p(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is continuous and differentiable on $(0,\\infty ).$ In particular, it is continuous on $[1,3]$ and differentiable on $(1,3).$ Therefore, $p(x)$ satisfies the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $q(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is continuous and differentiable on $(1,\\infty ).$ Given that it is not defined at $x=1,$ $q(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\n- The function $r(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is continuous and differentiable on $(-\\infty ,1)\\cup (1,\\infty ).$ Given that it is not defined at $x=1,$ $r(x)$ does not satisfy the conditions of the mean value theorem.\n\nTherefore, only function $p(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ satisfies the conditions for the mean value theorem over the interval $[1,3].$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262693 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175902 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "205c5518-c67a-5784-8cc7-55b42ce7fb0e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether the Extreme Value Theorem Is Applicable to a Function Given Its Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8239025-1548-543f-b742-41d95cf7deb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463628} {:answer/id #uuid "9a82f1b3-42a5-578c-8649-06dea016a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463629}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a82f1b3-42a5-578c-8649-06dea016a079" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 