nswer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667928} {:answer/id #uuid "aec76401-6965-5420-843a-8658c52bd156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667929}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9dee1e55-43de-5480-9c40-84d79de0f96f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667928} :answer-field/id #uuid "237ec551-87b0-5f9c-b83b-eeb721cff8d4" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "144d9fbc-7660-5ed9-9ae4-01d5a04d6a5a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127040" :question/problem "![](images/3c/3c25115cfb7ccde7ec0cbec249d62b037c7fb94be92905b186101ce1fd45a1d8.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above. On which interval is the extreme value theorem applicable to $f(x)?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the extreme value theorem is only applicable to closed intervals on which the function is continuous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's take a look at each interval.\n\n- The interval $[0,2]$ is closed, and the function is continuous on $[0,2].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\n- The interval $(1,2)$ is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $(-\\infty ,0]$ is closed, but it is not a bounded interval in the form $[a,b].$ Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[0,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262906 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices"}] :question/answ