rue" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd3030ea-f56b-54f2-b19e-0fe96063ba8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437792} :answer-field/id #uuid "10609156-1bc3-5176-82f7-7da72d8cac5c" :answer-field/key "$Q$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438925} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45f9eaa1-ec03-587f-9925-ac1e03ddc805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667930} {:answer/id #uuid "ceeca510-070e-5b7e-a5b0-fde585d5adcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceeca510-070e-5b7e-a5b0-fde585d5adcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667931} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceb5d4cf-1c76-560f-9b77-bb0950007541" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f86fe2f1-042a-5183-8a18-518a658cc1a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-128474" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $Q$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nQ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(Q) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(9-5)-1(6-3)-1(10-9) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4-3-1 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(Q)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, none of the statements are true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124475 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74f126da-5f3b-5af8-9aee-d6f0a4c61c49" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Shape of a Level Curve"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "179db532-d9e6-5e2e-91f3-aade01e0ddb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463676} {:answer/id #uuid "b3485b61-e757-5360-a24b-e5e8e1510cb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "179db532-d9e6-5e2e-91f3-aade01e0ddb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463676} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd745651-984a-5d60-a190-cb171692cead" :answer-field/key "$c=0$ gives a parabola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464772} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05537b17-7ec7-5fc9-bc2c-6afa58fbf701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463678} {:answer/id #uuid "503c7eee-dfea-59ab-9897-fba0a24aa061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05537b17-7ec7-5fc9-bc2c-6afa58fbf701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463678} :answer-field/id #uuid "538c309f-7174-5be3-8c40-ec951dfef7f2" :answer-field/key "$c=1$ gives an ellipse" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464773} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b488c30c-d8bb-5f46-b3aa-6f3e7348f877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463680} {:answer/id #uuid "0377582f-387c-5883-9a77-bf51a5c48a80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b488c30c-d8bb-5f46-b3aa-6f3e7348f877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463680} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bce9543-3652-5444-87d3-b92041c327f4" :answer-field/key "$c=2$ gives a hyperbola" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464774} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "020f95c1-ef74-5889-a12a-efb42904bfa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667934} {:answer/id #uuid "47c7001a-2548-5fbb-9908-60b15aab2a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47c7001a-2548-5fbb-9908-60b15aab2a6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186667935} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ae56a0e-a681-54cc-afc5-93a4cfff687c" :answer-field/key "None of the above" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186668244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b3926e5-b3cd-5c3a-a183-ad2104ed74d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-129062" :question/problem "The level curves of the function $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ are given by $f(x,y)=c.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Setting $f(x,y)=c$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} & =c \\\\ {y}^{2} & =c({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\ c{x}^{2}+(c-1){y}^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n- If $c=0,$ the level curve is the line $y=0,$ which is the $x$-axis. So, “$c=0$ gives a parabola” is false.\n\n- If $c=1,$ the level curve is the line $x=0,$ which is the $y$-axis. So, “$c=1$ gives an ellipse” is false.\n\n- If $c=2,$  then we obtain \n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}=2\\,⟹\\,2{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHowever, the only real solution to this equation is  $(x,y)=(0,0),$ which is not in the domain of $f(x,y)$ because it would result in division by zero. Thus, “$c=2$ gives a hyperbola” is false.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"None of the listed\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175903 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bbc6a2d-2078-50d5-9584-c705c19212da" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Intervals on Which a Given Function Satisfies the Extreme Value Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8d8437-9a1f-5e54-9c2d-9d69b5d07fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463682} {:answer/id #uuid "88820cc6-e369-5f61-8714-cccae1ecb7dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f8d8437-9a1f-5e54-9c2d-9d69b5d07fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :ans